  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab63eea9-f0b0-400d-89ce-38ff27cd56cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We are provided with code that performs clustering on the handwritten digits dataset using the K-Means algorithm grouping  them into 10 clusters, corresponding to the 10 digit classes. We are required to make the notebook work and test the characteristics of the K-Means Algorithm. We are also required to change the dataset and make adjustments on the given code to work with our new dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "**We are required to**\n",
    "\n",
    "i) make sure the code runs\n",
    "\n",
    "ii)Change some parameters on a given notebook and see the impact on the clustering process\n",
    "\n",
    "iii)Use another dataset and perform other operations, and simulate as an app\n",
    "\n",
    "**Changelog for K-Means Code**\n",
    "The given code worked well on my notebook after the installation of required libraries. I therefore\n",
    "\n",
    "**On the given Code and Generated data**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Changed number of clusters on a given code from 10 to 8 to see the impact\n",
    "\n",
    "**Replaced the Dataset and Adjusted the code**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Dataset Replacement:\n",
    "\n",
    "I loaded Iris Datset and replaced the Digits dataset by Replacing load_digits() with load_iris(). The original code used the digits dataset to cluster handwritten digits. The new version works with the Iris dataset to cluster flower species based on their features (sepal and petal dimensions).\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: The same loading procedure as previous dataset, Time spent: Approximately 10 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Data Initialization:\n",
    "\n",
    "I replaced digits.data and digits.target with iris.data and iris.target.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: 50%, Reason: unknown structure of the dataset which forced me to read about it, Time spent: Approximately 1 hour)*\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Number of Clusters:\n",
    "\n",
    "I djusted n_clusters from 10 to 3 in the KMeans initialization to match three distinct flower species (Setosa, Versicolor, and Virginica) of the Iris dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: Sources explained the concept well, Time spent: Approximately 10 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Cluster Center Visualization:\n",
    "\n",
    "I removed the visualization code for KMeans cluster centers using imshow() which was for images.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: Sources were clear on this, Time spent: Approximately 10 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Label Assignment:\n",
    "\n",
    "I replaced the loop over 10 clusters with a loop over 3 clusters and adjusted mask conditions accordingly.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: Straight forward replacement, Time spent: Approximately 10 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "6. User Input for Flower Features:\n",
    "\n",
    "I added a section to prompt the user to input sepal and petal dimensions (length and width) for a new flower. This new functionality allows the user to enter the dimensions of a new flower and use the trained KMeans model to predict the flower's type. This part did not exist in the original digits code.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: Did it with previous Models, Time spent: Approximately 10 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "7. New Data Point Prediction:\n",
    "\n",
    "I added code to create a new_flower array from the user inputs and predict its cluster using the trained KMeans model.\n",
    "After gathering input from the user, the model uses the KMeans predict() function to assign the new data point to one of the three clusters. This is a new feature to predict flower types, compared to the digits code, which only classified existing data points.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: 80%, Reason: I failed several times here due to failure to loop user inputs into cluster names, Time spent: Approximately 2 hours minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "8. Predicted Cluster Labeling:\n",
    "\n",
    "I used iris.target_names and the mode of iris_target for predicted clusters to determine the flower name. The clusters correspond to Iris flower species, so the mode of the target values is mapped to the appropriate flower name using iris.target_names.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Difficulty: 30%, Reason: Did it with previous Models, Time spent: Approximately <50 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "9. User Feedback:\n",
    "\n",
    "I added print statements to inform the user of the predicted flower type based on the model's output. The output of the model now includes user-friendly feedback displaying the predicted flower type (Setosa, Versicolor, or Virginica), as opposed to the accuracy metric from the digits code.\n",
    "\n",
    "*(Consider the difficulty and time as this is part of the above)*\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4d0a7990-070b-43f6-896e-e632f328cec5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Part A: Working with Given Code**\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5efa44b1-7d31-43f2-b399-7872c7233c56",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(i) *Making it work*\n",
    "\n",
    "The code run well after installing all the required libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1a1b08f5-cb3a-4d67-8d58-fea71386f01c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_digits\n",
    "\n",
    "digits = load_digits()\n",
    "digits.data.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=10, random_state=0)\n",
    "clusters = kmeans.fit_predict(digits.data)\n",
    "kmeans.cluster_centers_.shape\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 5, figsize=(8, 3))\n",
    "centers = kmeans.cluster_centers_.reshape(10, 8, 8)\n",
    "for axi, center in zip(ax.flat, centers):\n",
    "    axi.set(xticks=[], yticks=[])\n",
    "    axi.imshow(center, interpolation='nearest', cmap=plt.cm.binary)\n",
    "\n",
    "from scipy.stats import mode\n",
    "labels = np.zeros_like(clusters)\n",
    "for i in range(10):\n",
    "    mask = (clusters == i)\n",
    "    labels[mask] = mode(digits.target[mask])[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
    "accuracy_score(digits.target, labels)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4107d205-5264-4bdb-b659-d0c79ba56f52",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ii) *Change some parameters and see the impact*\n",
    "\n",
    "In this case, I changed the number of clusters from 10 to 8, accuracy dropped from 0.7440 to 0.6466 suggesting that it is not a good cluster size for the numbers provided"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4c80d0a6-c8e2-4eb0-b731-764f5f899320",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_digits\n",
    "\n",
    "digits = load_digits()\n",
    "\n",
    "kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=8, random_state=0)  # Adjusted number of clusters to 8\n",
    "clusters = kmeans.fit_predict(digits.data)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 4, figsize=(8, 3))  # Adjusted for 8 clusters\n",
    "centers = kmeans.cluster_centers_.reshape(8, 8, 8)  # Adjusted for 8 clusters\n",
    "for axi, center in zip(ax.flat, centers):\n",
    "    axi.set(xticks=[], yticks=[])\n",
    "    axi.imshow(center, interpolation='nearest', cmap=plt.cm.binary)\n",
    "\n",
    "from scipy.stats import mode\n",
    "labels = np.zeros_like(clusters)\n",
    "for i in range(8):  # Adjusted for 8 clusters\n",
    "    mask = (clusters == i)\n",
    "    labels[mask] = mode(digits.target[mask])[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score # Calculate the accuracy score\n",
    "accuracy_score(digits.target, labels)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d5597f8-8f98-48f5-ad88-1865f996033f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Part B: Working with Another Dataset**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "052dc195-273d-4d26-9885-5186438fbe11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "I will use the Iris dataset\n",
    "The Iris dataset consists of 150 samples from three iris flower species: Setosa, Versicolor, and Virginica. Each sample has four features—sepal length, sepal width, petal length, and petal width— measured in centimeters. The label values will therefore be Setosa, Versicolor, and Virginica "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6bda6e20-a306-4dde-b18a-8c4f45e8e742",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "i)**Model training and testing accuracy**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4509a5e9-441b-43ac-8550-e03f28753f47",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Step 1: Loading libraries and Iris dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c85440be-403e-4dd3-a10a-b75f58daaf55",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
    "from scipy.stats import mode\n",
    "\n",
    "iris = load_iris()\n",
    "iris_data = iris.data\n",
    "iris_target = iris.target"
   ]
  },
